# Google OAuth client ID for sign-in.
#
# Create one at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   1. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type "Web application".
#   2. Add your origins under "Authorised JavaScript origins", e.g.
#        http://localhost:5173
#        https://your-deployed-domain.example
#      (origins only — Google Identity Services does not use redirect URIs here.)
#   3. Copy the client ID below. It is a public value and safe to ship in the
#      bundle; there is no client secret in this flow.
#
# Leave unset to run Prepology exactly as before, with accounts disabled.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in the value.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
